people are really different. Well, robots are even more different than different people. So the first question then is, do we need a whole new psychology, a whole new psychology, understand social responses to social robots? And the answer, when we look at the literature, is pretty clearly no. People tend to bring sort of standard social psychological processes to new media. So there's tons of work that shows that we treat technology. kind of as social actors. And we bring our old brain, which has been evolving for a long time to understand

