down to the low, low space, and stereotypes down there would be poor people. So this would be poor white, poor black, homeless, people on welfare. And, um, and, um, And they evoke a different kind of emotion as well, which is contempt. And so you keep going around, you get up to the high, warmth, low competence. These are people in the 90s would be like housewives, people in that sort of space, you know, mentally handicapped individuals, you know. So again, these are stereotypes. Yeah.

