And programmed to lie to humans. And so, I mean, it's really fascinating. And so you know the engineers used robotics when they were developing this? Well, we don't know that, but we can kind of think of the car a little bit like a robot, right? It's a technology that it wasn't. making its own decision, it was programmed in, but it was programmed by humans to lie to humans via, you know, its sort of technology. So, right, what's going to happen with robots? We've seen some autonomous robots that have learned to lie. So these are small little robots, and their

